I think a better way to increase monks fighting is to realize that
hands become better weapon as you gain skill with them. So that
unskilled fighters both normal and martial do d2 damage. While
characters with martial skill grow their fist power by 1 every skill,
normals grow by 1 every alternate skill. So that we get the following
(the +x is the skill damage)

skill               normal          martial
unskilled           d2+0            d2+0
basic                d2+1            d3+1
skilled              d3+1             d4+2
expert              d3+2             d5+3
master             d4+2             d6+4
GM                  d4+3             d7+5

I think monks should get extra 1 point of damage per skill.
And would get no skill damage when wearing an armour, so that the
damage is d7 only,
at GM level.
Also against any thick skinned creature, the damage should be divided
by two.

A martial reaching skilled should also be able to hit with both hands,
without the need to use two weaponing.

